vmhal3d (JHRobotics/vmhal9x 8bc480e) MesaBufferTexturesChanges: a FBHDA_DD_DELETE
notification is handled at the next draw, when its dxid may already belong to a surface
created after the deleted one (Dungeon Keeper 2 streams its textures). Destroying by dxid
then took the NEW texture's record: white, untextured walls and HUD. Now a DELETE destroys
only while the dxid still maps to the deleted record; otherwise the stale record is just
unlinked and freed. This path never ran before nvmini.vxd 3121: the VxD's
FBHDA_DD_surface_set returned uid 0 for every new surface (upstream vmdisp9x does too), so
no dd_fifo item ever matched and texture updates after the first upload never reached GL
(Dungeon Keeper 2's menu text tiles showed other textures). Apply after vmhal-depthfill.patch.

--- a/mesa3d_buffer.c
+++ b/mesa3d_buffer.c
@@ -649,7 +649,20 @@
 						} // loop ddsurf = ddsurf->up
 						break;
 					case FBHDA_DD_DELETE:
-						MesaBufferTextureDestroy(ctx, ddsurf->dxid);
+						/* notifications are handled at the next draw: by then the dxid may
+						 * belong to a surface created after this one was deleted (Dungeon
+						 * Keeper 2 streams its textures); destroying by dxid would take the
+						 * new texture's record - only drop this stale record then */
+						if(ddsurf->dxid == 0 || ddsurf_get_by_id(ctx, ddsurf->dxid) == ddsurf)
+						{
+							MesaBufferTextureDestroy(ctx, ddsurf->dxid);
+						}
+						else
+						{
+							ddsurf_unpair(ddsurf);
+							ht_delete_more(entry->ht_flat, DW_FLAT(ddsurf->flatptr), ddsurf);
+							hal3d_free((void**)&ddsurf);
+						}
 						break;
 				}
 				break;
